    "result_text": "All 282 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-registration cap: creating an owner is rejected with **400 Bad Request** once 20 owners already exist with today's registration date.\n\nThree changes, following the existing `DuplicateOwnerException` pattern in the codebase:\n\n1. **`DailyOwnerRegistrationLimitExceededException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` signaling the daily limit was hit.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 for new owners, after the duplicate checks and before assigning a registration date, it calls `hasReachedDailyRegistrationLimit()`, which counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws when the count is \u2265 `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY` (20). Placing the check before the registration date is defaulted means the new owner isn't counted against itself.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 a new `@ExceptionHandler` maps the exception to HTTP 400 with a `ProblemDetail` body, consistent with the other handlers.\n\nThe `Cp13Tests` acceptance test (20 creates succeed, 21st returns 400) passes, along with the full suite of 282 tests. Seed owners have a null `registration_date`, so they don't count toward today's total.",
